**`go/ast/inspector/inspector.go`** — added `Len()` method (lines 229–238):

```go
// Len returns the number of AST nodes the inspector holds,
// the same number that ast.Inspect visits over the files given to New.
func (in *Inspector) Len() int {
	n := 0
	for i := int32(0); i < int32(len(in.events)); i++ {
		if in.events[i].index > i {
			n++
		}
	}
	return n
}
```

It counts **push events** — those where `index > i` (push events point forward to their matching pop, while pop events point backward). This matches the count `ast.Inspect` visits.

**`go/ast/inspector/inspector_test.go`** — added `TestLen` which parses a small AST, counts nodes via `ast.Inspect`, and asserts `inspect.Len()` matches.

